div.div:
synăloephē  (-līphē , -loepha ), ēs,
		f., = συναλοιφή,

I.the contraction of
				two syllables into one, either by synæresis or by
			crasis; 
				“in later gram. applied esp. to elision, =
					collisio, elisio,”
				 Quint. 9, 4, 109
			; Charis. p. 249 P.;
					Diom. p. 437 ib.;
					Mart. Cap. 3, § 267;
					Serv. Verg. A. 2, 16.
